Package: immunoTriage
Type: Package
Title: Benchmarking Immune Gene-Expression Signatures Against Matched Random
    Gene Sets, with Cell-Type Attribution and Triage
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("dryichen", role = c("aut","cre"),
    email = "200455590+dryichen@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Tools to evaluate immune gene-expression signatures honestly.
    Signatures are scored with the method used in their original publication (GSVA,
    ssGSEA, or weighted mean) and compared against a random-gene-set null matched on
    gene-set size and scoring engine, alongside confounder controls (proliferation,
    hypoxia, chromosomal instability) that a genuinely immune-specific result must
    outperform. A signature's expected behavior is predicted from the cell types its
    signal comes from, using any single-cell reference atlas with cell-type
    annotation; the model shipped here was trained on a gastric atlas, its predictions
    were locked before an external validation in cohorts it had never seen, and its
    behavior under a second, lung atlas is reported in the accompanying paper. The package also estimates the information ceiling of a
    dataset by fitting penalized and ensemble models under grouped cross-validation.
